%
%  The value at the END of each variable can be modified according
%  to your requirements. When the XMSG system needs to be changed,
%  the XMSG installation program (XMSG-IN-L:PROG) can read the
%  system definitions from this file and modify the XMSG system.
%  (The "old" value is the value in DECIMAL at the time the file was written.)
%
%  IMPORTANT:
%     a) The XMSG product files must have been installed properly.
%     b) Own access to (UTILITY)XMSG-SYS-DEF-L:SYMB must be RWAD.
%     c) Do NOT remove any line(s) on this file.
%     d) Do NOT insert or append any extra line(s) on this file.
%     e) Do NOT change any line in this heading.
%     f) Do NOT rename any XMSG variable name.
%     g) Do NOT insert, remove or change any character preceding
%        the system variable value at the end of each line.
%     h) Replace the value at the END of each variable with
%        your new definition.
%
X4TSK, Maximum number of task descriptors__________________(old: 80):80
X5PRT, Maximum number of ports_____________________________(old: 128):128
X4NAM, Maximum number of named systems/ports_______________(old: 768):768
X4NLW, Maximum length of name in words_____________________(old: 16):16
X4MES, Maximum number of message elements__________________(old: 256):256
X4MMX, Maximum message size in bytes_______________________(old: 2500):2500
X5MTS, Maximum buffer space owned by a task in bytes_______(old: 12500):12500
X4BPG, Message buffer space in pages_______________________(old: 25):25
X4MCB, Maximum number of calls in a multicall function_____(old: 5):5
X4SIR, Maximum number of systems accessible________________(old: 512):512
X5LNK, Maximum number of links_____________________________(old: 4):4
X4LTO, Default HDLC/Megalink timeout in XTUs_______________(old: 10):10
X5TO1, Timeout in XTUs when receiving datagrams____________(old: 150):150
X5TO2, Timeout in XTUs when transmitting datagrams_________(old: 200):200
X3FSZ, Maximum frame size in words (input)_________________(old: 312):312
X4FSO, Maximum frame size in words (output)________________(old: 312):312
X4ACK, Maximum number of network acknowledgement frames____(old: 15):15
X4NBF, Default number of receive frames per link___________(old: 5):5
X4TMS, Number of transmit buffers per network server_______(old: 2):2
X4IRM, Default maximum number of SABMs when starting link__(old: 10):10
X4RPM, Maximum number of repeats before link is stopped____(old: 5):5
X4MXH, Maximum number of hops allowed______________________(old: 20):20
X5NGT, Gateway timeout in XTUs when sending to net server__(old: 50):50
X5TRB, Number of trace buffers_____________________________(old: 2):2
